# Names-only template. Uncomment and populate only the entries needed for this workflow.
# No defaults or credential values are provided. Optional unset variables retain code defaults.
# Names-only template. Uncomment and populate only the entries needed for this workflow.
# No defaults or credential values are provided. Optional unset variables retain code defaults.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# USDC Lending Strategy — SHADOW deployment profile
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy to .env.shadow and fill in, then run:
#   ./script/deploy-usdc-lending-shadow.sh            # preflight + dry-run
#   ./script/deploy-usdc-lending-shadow.sh --broadcast
#
# "Shadow" = an Arbitrum One environment that mirrors mainnet state (a hosted
# fork, or a local `anvil --fork-url <arbitrum> --chain-id 42161`). The strategy
# REUSES UsdcLendingConfigArbitrum for every protocol venue + Permit2, and
# expects Multyr core to already exist at its Arbitrum mainnet addresses.
#
# The runner does NOT modify DeployUsdcLendingStrategy.s.sol. It wraps it:
#   1. PreflightUsdcLendingShadow   — read-only checks, before any tx
#   2. DeployUsdcLendingStrategy    — the unmodified production deploy script
#   3. PostflightUsdcLendingShadow  — verify wiring/roles + write the manifest
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Environment identity (must be exactly "shadow") ─────────────────────────
# DEPLOY_ENV=

# ── Shadow RPC (the ONLY rpc used — no fallback to a production RPC_URL) ─────
# SHADOW_RPC_URL=

# ── Shadow deployer key — NOT named DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY (the runner rejects
#    that name in .env.shadow to keep a production key out) ──────────────────
# SHADOW_DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Optional: comma-separated addresses that must NEVER be the Shadow deployer
# (paste your production deployer address here).
# FORBIDDEN_DEPLOYER_ADDRESSES=

# ── Shadow governance / operator addresses (all required, nonzero, distinct) ─
# SHADOW_GUARDIAN_ADDRESS=
# SHADOW_GOVERNANCE_ADDRESS=
# SHADOW_KEEPER_ADDRESS=
                                 #   keeper's role grants are a governance decision;
                                 #   StrategyUpkeep is deployed + granted KEEPER_ROLE)
# SHADOW_EMERGENCY_ADDRESS=

# ── Multyr core on the Shadow fork (Arbitrum mainnet addresses) ─────────────
# VAULT_ADDRESS=
# STRATEGY_ROUTER_ADDRESS=
# BUFFER_MANAGER_ADDRESS=
# HEALTH_REGISTRY_ADDRESS=

# ── Optional: final seal / ownership handoff ───────────────────────────────
# DO_SEAL=
# SELECTOR_REGISTRY_ADDRESS=
# SYSTEM_SEALER_ADDRESS=

# ── Optional: deploy flags (defaults shown) ────────────────────────────────
# DEPLOY_UPKEEP=
# DEPLOY_LENDING_ADAPTERS=
# UNPAUSE_BUFFER=
# ADAPTER_MAX_EXPOSURE_BPS=

# ── Optional: pin a deployment id (default: <utc-timestamp>-<git-sha>) ──────
# Artifacts land under deployments/shadow/<SHADOW_DEPLOYMENT_ID>/.
# SHADOW_DEPLOYMENT_ID=

# ── Optional: EVM version override for a LOCAL anvil Shadow fork ────────────
# Production/foundry.toml is "cancun". anvil forking Arbitrum with --hardfork
# cancun is broken (Arbitrum blocks carry no EIP-4844 blob-gas fields), so a
# local anvil Shadow fork must run `--hardfork shanghai` and this must match:
# SHADOW_EVM_VERSION=
# A hosted Shadow RPC needs no override — leave blank.
# SHADOW_EVM_VERSION=
